# S04: Event-Grained Purchase Ledger and Line Composition

> *«CRM не хранит "Павлик купил пятую шаверму" как одно большое текстовое поле. Она хранит
> отдельное событие покупки, связанное с ID клиента.»*

## Objective

Change the identity of an order line from `(order_id, menu_item_id)` to its own UUID plus a
composition hash, so two differently-composed portions of the same dish can coexist. Capture
modifiers and guest notes as structured data. Record every order mutation as an append-only event
instead of overwriting state and clobbering a single `notes` string.

## The blocking gap this closes

A line's identity **is** `(order_id, menu_item_id)` today. Both add paths *merge* quantities
(`items.post.ts:120` `existingItem.quantity + quantity`; `items-batch.post.ts:76-80` pre-collapses
duplicates in a Map). "Steak, rare" and "Steak, well-done" are structurally impossible. A grep for
`modifier|option|extra|sauce|customiz` across the orders domain returns only HTML `<option>`
elements.

Without this sprint, P3's *"с каким соусом чаще всего заказывают?"* is not merely unimplemented —
it is unanswerable, and S05's per-modifier ingredient consumption has nothing to key on.

