## Breaking-change register

The wire identity of an order line changes from `menu_item_id` to `order_items.id`. Affected:
`orders.get.ts:121`, `orders.post.ts:233`, `orders/[id].put.ts:418`, `item-status.put.ts`,
`decline-item.post.ts`, `items.post.ts`, `items-batch.post.ts`, `composables/useOrders.ts`, and
the `:key` bindings in `components/order/OrderItems.vue:11` and `components/OrderCard.vue:126`.
This violates no locked invariant but invalidates an assumption baked into every order surface.

## Definition of Done

- [ ] Two portions of the same dish with different modifiers coexist on one order, can be
      declined and progressed independently, and render separately
- [ ] Every order mutation writes an `order_events` row with actor attribution
- [ ] No feature writes a machine-readable prefix into a `notes` column (retires the
      `REFUND_REQUESTED:` hack from S02 finding #1)
- [ ] Modifier surcharges survive every subsequent item mutation
- [ ] `GET /api/guests/[id]/purchases` returns datetime, amount, composition, chosen modifier and
      payment method per purchase — the article's literal purchase-event record
- [ ] The index swap from two-column to three-column identity succeeds against a production restore
- [ ] **Owner-visible deliverable:** order timeline replaces the overwritten notes string

## Invariants Produced

1. An order line is identified by `order_items.id` on the wire and by
   `(order_id, menu_item_id, composition_hash)` in the database. `menu_item_id` alone is never a
   line identifier again.
2. `order_items.notes` is operator free text only; decline state lives in
   `declined_at`/`declined_by`.
3. `order_items.guest_note` is the only per-line customer text field.
4. Every mutating order route calls `recordOrderEvent`. `order_events` is the single fan-out seam
   for downstream domains (S06's rules engine hangs off it).
5. `order_events` is append-only — no UPDATE or DELETE policy may ever be added.
6. Line money is `base_price + modifier_total`, maintained by `recalc_order_line_totals()`.
   Application code must never recompute an order total from `price * quantity` again.
7. `order_items.id` is the stable `source_id` that S05 stock movements reference.
8. Migration numbering continues at **040**.
